  "description": "<p>Established in 2005, Heriot-Watt University Dubai is a satellite campus of Heriot-Watt University situated in Dubai, United Arab Emirates. Significantly, it was one of the first campuses of an overseas university to open in Dubai International Academic City.&nbsp;</p><p>A world class institution, it is a leading business school with recruitment partnerships to support students as they enter the world of employment. 30,000 students of this renowned university study worldwide, making it a truly international place to study programmes such as engineering, food science, fashion and more.</p><h2>What is the Heriot-Watt University Dubai acceptance rate for International Students?</h2><p>The Heriot-Watt University Dubai acceptance rate is 24%.</p> <p>Heriot-Watt University Dubai has state-of-the-art ICT and computer rooms, spacious classrooms and a library that connects students to higher learning materials and a wealth of resources. Counselling services are also available to provide pastoral support and the many restaurants around the site are in close proximity to campus.</p><p>No university would be complete without common room areas for socializing, relaxing or joint study to make it more exciting, and thatâ€™s what Heriot-Watt University Dubai provides. There is an in-house engineering laboratory for use by mechanical engineering students that enhances their ability to learn the subject.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>The university encourages students to get involved with the many student clubs and support services dotted around campus at Heriot-Watt University Dubai. From a model United Nations society to a music club for those with rhythm, there is a lot of activity going on. The student council is active and there is even an anime and gaming club due to how diverse the interests of the students on campus are. Several sports clubs are available for students to join so they can participate in group sports and bond with like-minded people.&nbsp;</p><p>A provider hub for volunteering opportunities also exists on campus and there is also a free student wellbeing service for students who need mental health support.</p>",
